# Intentional architectural exceptions for Trivy IaC security scanning (decision 0030).
# Every entry below is documented with its architectural reason.

# 1. Initial bootstrap before enable_hardening = true:
# Stage 1 starts with public_network_access_enabled = true on Nerdio's Key Vault, SQL Server, and
# Storage so the first deploy and Nerdio's initial setup wizard can run before Private Endpoints and
# the VNet runner are switched on in the second apply (enable_hardening = true).
AVD-AZU-0013
AVD-AZU-0016
AVD-AZU-0022
AVD-AZU-0026

# 2. Key Vault purge protection and key expiration:
# Purge protection defaults to false on sandbox/dev so trial deployments can be torn down cleanly
# without stranding Key Vault names for 90 days; production enables it via nerdio_core.purge_protection_enabled
# and modules/cmk-encryption always sets purge_protection_enabled = true.
# Data-protection wrapping keys (DataProtection-main, openbao-unseal) do not set a fixed expiration
# date because expiring an active wrapping key without an application re-wrap bricks encrypted data.
AVD-AZU-0014
AVD-AZU-0015
AVD-AZU-0017

# 3. Storage Account network rules & logging:
# State storage (modules/deploy-pipeline) and Nerdio data-protection storage use Entra OAuth only
# (shared_access_key_enabled = false, allow_nested_items_to_be_public = false) and must be reachable
# by GitHub OIDC / Cloud Shell during bootstrap.
AVD-AZU-0010
AVD-AZU-0011
AVD-AZU-0012

# 4. SQL Server auditing / threat detection:
# Nerdio Manager's SQL database holds application state and is monitored via Nerdio's own Log
# Analytics workspace and Application Insights; extra SQL Storage Auditing accounts are not required.
AVD-AZU-0023
AVD-AZU-0024
AVD-AZU-0025
AVD-AZU-0027

# 5. NSG outbound service tags & OpenBao HTTPS ingress:
# Session host NSGs allow outbound TCP 443 to WindowsVirtualDesktop and AzureCloud service tags and
# TCP 1688 to Azure KMS; OpenBao allows TCP 8200 from var.allowed_source_addresses (configurable CIDR).
AVD-AZU-0047
AVD-AZU-0048
AVD-AZU-0050
AVD-AZU-0051

# 6. Linux VM / VMSS SSH keys on ephemeral cloud-init or managed-identity workers:
# modules/openbao and modules/automation-workers disable SSH and password login completely; all
# configuration is declarative via cloud-init or Azure VM extensions.
AVD-AZU-0038
AVD-AZU-0039

# 7. GitHub repository & Actions environment metadata:
# - modules/github-settings manages the public open-source template repository (visibility is configurable via var.repo.visibility).
# - modules/deploy-pipeline stores non-secret Azure identifiers (ARM_TENANT_ID, ARM_SUBSCRIPTION_ID, ARM_CLIENT_ID,
#   TFSTATE_RESOURCE_GROUP, TFSTATE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT) in github_actions_environment_secret so GitHub Actions masks
#   real GUIDs in workflow logs per Guardrail 4; no actual credentials or keys are stored there (authentication is OIDC).
AVD-GIT-0001
AVD-GIT-0002
AVD-GIT-0003
